tsford–Mission","y":1.8,"placeId":"abbotsford-mission"},{"x":"Fredericton","y":1.8,"placeId":"fredericton"},{"x":"Charlottetown","y":1.8,"placeId":"charlottetown"},{"x":"Moncton","y":2.3,"placeId":"moncton"},{"x":"Windsor","y":1.6,"placeId":"windsor"},{"x":"Yellowknife","y":5.6,"placeId":"yellowknife"}]}],"notes":"Universe: employed labour force aged 15+ with a usual place of work (excludes people working at home or with no fixed workplace). Census day was in May 2021, during COVID-19 restrictions. Other = 100% minus car, transit and walk/bicycle (motorcycle, taxi and other methods). Places ordered by transit share; places missing any share are omitted.","sourceIds":["statcan-98-10-0457-01"]}],"interpretation":["If you do not speak French, the Quebec places are the hardest to navigate in everyday settings, even though bilingualism is common in Montréal and the Gatineau part of Ottawa-Gatineau; outside Quebec, Moncton, Sudbury and Ottawa are the places where French is most usable in daily life.","Commute patterns reflect urban form: transit commuting is concentrated in the three largest metros, while in most other places the car dominates and long commutes are uncommon. Use this with rent data to judge whether living near work is affordable.","These are area-wide shares (metropolitan area or agglomeration). Neighbourhood patterns within a metro, for example downtown versus suburbs, can differ sharply."],"methodology":["Statistics Canada 2021 Census tables 98-10-0175-01 (knowledge of official languages), 98-10-0227-01 (language most often at home), 98-10-0457-01 (main mode and duration of commuting), 98-10-0308-01 (immigrant status) and 98-10-0038-01 (household size), each filtered to the place's CMA/CA DGUID (Ottawa and Gatineau: Ontario and Quebec parts).","Percentages are computed from published counts using the totals for all ages and genders; long-form counts are randomly rounded by Statistics Canada, so small differences (about one percentage point) should not be over-read."],"limitations":["Long-form census data come from a 25% sample (household size and population from 100% data).","Language knowledge is self-reported and covers all ages, including young children; it is not a measure of fluency at work.","Commuting universe: employed labour force aged 15+ with a usual place of work (excludes those working at home or with no fixed workplace). The census was taken in May 2021 under COVID-19 restrictions, which depressed transit use.","Iqaluit is a single municipality outside any CMA/CA and has no value for these metrics in this version."],"sourceIds":["statcan-98-10-0038-01","statcan-98-10-0175-01","statcan-98-10-0227-01","statcan-98-10-0457-01"],"relatedPlaceIds":["toronto","montreal","vancouver","calgary","edmonton","ottawa","gatineau","winnipeg","quebec-city","hamilton","kitchener-waterloo","london","halifax","victoria","saskatoon","regina","st-johns","windsor","kelowna","abbotsford-mission","moncton","saint-john","fredericton","sherbrooke","sudbury","thunder-bay","charlottetown","brandon","whitehorse","yellowknife","iqaluit"],"computedAt":"2026-11-05"}